  "weeklyExtras": {
    "week": 11,
    "tagline": "Week 11 News · Spartan Revenge · West Coast Panic · Three Weeks Left",
    "kicker": "GFL Insider · Week 11",
    "headline": "BARTON CAME BACK WITH A VENGEANCE. THE WILD WEST FORGOT HOW TO WIN.",
    "deck": "One week after scoring 151.66 and getting nothing for it, Barton smashed the league leader with 148.16. Off Boys stole a 1.10-point thriller, Space Cadets mugged the West leader with 78 points, and suddenly three weeks is not nearly enough breathing room.",
    "story": [
      "Matt Kitson apparently spent the week angry. After scoring 151.66 in Week 10 and somehow losing, THE Barton Spartans came back with 148.16, the highest score of Week 11, and flattened first-place Turbulent Ticklesh!ts 148.16-87.66. Jonah Coleman erupted for 32.9, Patrick Mahomes added 24.96 and Travis Kelce chipped in 22.4. Barton is only 3-8, but 299.82 points across the last two weeks is the kind of dead-team behavior that ruins somebody else's December.",
      "The Wild West turned into a bar fight where everybody missed. California entered 8-2 and scored 74.70. Redwood had a chance to capitalize and lost 112.26-111.16 to Off Boys by 1.10. Eskimo Brothers lost to Flint. The only West team that actually improved its position was Kyle O'Connell's Off Boys, now 6-5 after a third straight win. California still leads at 8-3 and Redwood sits 7-4, but the division suddenly has teeth everywhere instead of a clean two-team race.",
      "Out East, the Beasts kept feeding. Simpson Sith followed the Week 10 nuclear blast with a much quieter 104.26-96.62 win over Your Mom, while Sullco stopped the Medford freight train 105.70-87.74. Danny and Owen both sit 7-4, separated by scoring strength more than record. Simpson owns 1,247.34 PF, second in the league; Sullco sits at 1,192.72. Three weeks left, same record, no room for politeness.",
      "Flint keeps clawing out of the grave. Stephen started 0-6. The Tropics are now 4-7 after beating Eskimo Brothers 102.04-89.50, with CeeDee Lamb putting up 24.7 and Bucky Irving 17.5. Flint's season has been one long argument between record and performance; the record is finally beginning to lose that argument.",
      "And Space Cadets produced the week's funniest upset: 78.08 points, second-lowest score in the league, and a win over 8-2 California because Tavis managed only 74.70. James Cook III led Kris with 16.2. It was not beautiful, but beauty does not show up in the standings. At 4-7, Space Cadets found exactly the kind of ugly win that keeps the lights on."
    ],
    "awards": [
      {
        "emoji": "⚔️",
        "title": "Revenge Tour",
        "team": "THE Barton Spartans",
        "detail": "148.16, Week 11 high points, and a 60.50-point demolition of first-place Ticklesh!ts. Matt followed the cruelest loss of the season by kicking in the front door."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "🩸",
        "title": "One-Point Heist",
        "team": "Off Boys",
        "detail": "112.26-111.16 over Redwood. A 1.10-point margin turns Kyle into a 6-5 problem and leaves Collin with a third loss in four weeks."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "🛸",
        "title": "Ugly Counts",
        "team": "Space Cadets",
        "detail": "78.08 was only 3.38 points above California, but it was enough. Kris beat the West leader while posting the second-lowest score of Week 11. Fantasy football has no style points."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "🧟",
